[For "black"]
[Kind "main"]
[Start "qg-declined-main 3...Nf6"]
[Name "The Declined: 4.Nf3"]

4. Nf3 { Develops, and White has not yet said where the c1 bishop goes. }
4... Be7 { Black's set-up does not depend on what White does: the bishop goes to e7 and the king castles. Many players pin with 4...Bb4 instead, but that is a different plan to learn. }
5. Bg5 { The pin, one move later than in the main line. }
5... O-O { The bishop is already on e7, so there is no pin to worry about, and Black can castle. }
6. e3 { The main line again, with a different move order. Black plays 6...Nbd7 as before. } *
